{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>Every man upon his service, and upon his burden, and his appointed charge.</b> He assigned each of them to the service he would perform at the time of encampment, and to his burden at the time of journeying, so that he would know how much his burden weighed. He would also know his appointed charge — that is, he would know the names of the vessels he was to carry, which are designated by name, as it says: וּבְשֵׁמֹת תִּפְקְדוּ אֶת כְּלֵי מִשְׁמֶרֶת מַשָּׂאָם (Numbers 4:32)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:38.665110334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}